Pattern values narrowed beneath a struct the lens does not map: the finding
is at the pattern, which names no field to copy on its own, so the struct is
copied whole and reported as a whole. A copy field by field would copy
nothing, and drop every value without an error.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		[string]: string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		[string]: "a"
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		id: v0_0.id
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		[string]: "a"
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens in history/1.0.thema would copy v0_0.meta into meta, which does not accept every value of it
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:1
  |
8 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both 0.0 and 1.0 declare meta, so a lens that does not map it copies it
  = note: meta.[_] in 1.0 is now "a", which does not accept every value of the prior string
  = help: map meta in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
